ENTRY            22098   20171107   20180917   20180917       2267
SUBENT        22098001   20171107   20180917   20180917       2267
BIB                 14         76
TITLE       Neutron elastic and inelastic scattering from carbon
            in the energy range 16.5-22.0 MeV
AUTHOR     (N.Olsson,B.Trostell,E.Ramstroem)
REFERENCE  (J,NP/A,496,505,1989) - final publ.
           (C,88MITO,,1045,1988) - data on figs
           (J,NIM/A,245,415,1986) - description of experiment and
            data at En = 21.6 MeV.
INSTITUTE  (2SWDSWR)
FACILITY   (VDG,2SWDSWR) Studsvik 6 MV van de Graaff accelerator,
            equipped with a terminal pulsing and klystron bunching
            system, as well as a post-acceleration bunching system
            Delivered bursts of 1.5 - 5.5 MeV deuterons at a
            repetition rate of 1 MHz with a pulse width at half
            maximum of less than 0.3 ns and an average beam
            current of 3 microAmps.
INC-SOURCE (D-T) Target cell of length 1.0 or 2.0 cm filled with
            tritium gas to a pressure of up to 4 atm. The
            molybdenum entrance window of the cell had a thickness
            of 4 mg/cm2, and was clamped with 0.1 mm thick indium
            O-rings between slightly inclined surfaces. The total
            energy spread was estimated to Be less than +/- 0.1
            MeV at 22.0 MeV neutron energy, increasing to about
            +/- 0.3 MeV at 16.5 MeV.
METHOD     (TOF) Time-of-flight with flight path of 3.5 - 4 m.
            Total time resolution was about 1 ns for elastic
            scattering at 22 MeV, increasing to 2 ns at 16.5 MeV,
            corresponding to a resolution of 0.8 and 1.0 MeV,
            respectively.
DETECTOR   (SCIN) Two identical 12.7 cm diameter by 5.1 cm thick
            NE213 liquid scintillators, mounted on fast photo-
            multiplier tubes, were used to measure the angular
            distributions of scattered neutrons. The detectors
            were separated by 5 degrees and were positioned in a
            heavy shielding. With a lower level discriminator set
            at 3 MeV neutron energy, excellent n-gamma discrimi-
            nation and intrinsic time resolution was obtained. A
            70 cm long Hevimet shadow bar protected the detectors
            from the direct target flux. The system could be
            rotated on a circular track with an angular precision
            of about 0.2 degrees.
           (SCIN) The relative neutron flux was determined using
            a TOF neutron monitor consisting of a 5 cm diameter by
            5 cm thick plastic scintillator.
MONITOR    (1-H-1(N,EL)1-H-1,,DA)
MONIT-REF  (,J.C.Hopkins+,J,ND/A,9,137,1971) Lrl constrained phase
            shifts.
SAMPLE     .Hollow cylinder of 5.0 cm height, outer diameter of
            2.5 cm and inner diameter of 1.0 cm, being of a
            natural isotopic composition and a chemical purity of
            close to 100%.
            The monitor target was a parallelepiped polyethylene
            sample with the dimensions 5.0 x 2.5 x 0.8 cm.
            The samples were positioned at a distance of 14.5 cm
            in front of the target.
CORRECTION .Corrections were applied for the variation of the
            detector efficiency with energy, anisotropy of the
            neutrons from the D-T reaction, finite scattering
            geometry, flux attenuation and multiple scattering.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-1) Counting statistics in the H(n,n)H measurements
           (ERR-3) Uncertainty due to correction factor for
            the polyethylene sample
           (ERR-4) Uncertainty in differential H(n,n)H cr.section
           (ERR-5,2.0,10.0) Uncertainty due to relative efficiency
           of the neutron detectors:
                Ex             %
                 0.0        2.0
                 4.44       2.0 - 3.5
                 7.65       2.0 - 5.0
                 9.64       3.5 - 10.0
HISTORY    (19881031C) N.O.
           (19890530U) IF. Page of reference added
           (20171107A) SD:Updated to new date formats,lower case.
           Refs NIM/A, NP/A were added. Subents 006-007 were added
           ERR-ANALYS update and moved to Subents 002-005.
           Subents 006,007 with kerma factors added.
           EN-ERR moved to Sub.002.
ENDBIB              76
